                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "f2d9349f-1ac2-4926-a545-cb339b7c2a28",
                          "text": "文档: The class `OfNat α n` powers the numeric literal parser. If you write `37 : α`,…",
                          "children": [],
                          "isExpanded": true,
                          "parentId": "08905b11-c276-483c-9d84-c8da230a4eec",
                          "data": {
                            "note": "**文档**\n\nThe class `OfNat α n` powers the numeric literal parser. If you write\n`37 : α`, Lean will attempt to synthesize `OfNat α 37`, and will generate\nthe term `(OfNat.ofNat 37 : α)`.\n\nThere is a bit of infinite regress here since the desugaring apparently\nstill contains a literal `37` in it. The type of expressions contains a\nprimitive constructor for \"raw natural number literals\", which you can directly\naccess using the macro `nat_lit 37`. Raw number literals are always of type `Nat`.\nSo it would be more correct to say that Lean looks for an instance of\n`OfNat α (nat_lit 37)`, and it generates the term `(OfNat.ofNat (nat_lit 37) : α)`.",
                            "tags": [
                              "attribute",
                              "文档"
                            ]
                          },
                          "style": {
                            "background": "#f9fafb",
                            "color": "#6b7280",
                            "fontSize": 11,
                            "borderColor": "#e5e7eb"
                          }
                        }
                      ],
                      "isExpanded": false,
                      "parentId": "0b9a3307-3129-4a1f-a15c-497d3a93d2f0",
                      "data": {
                        "tags": [
                          "attribute-group"
                        ]
                      },
                      "style": {
                        "background": "#f3f4f6",
                        "color": "#4b5563",
                        "fontSize": 12,
                        "shape": "round",
                        "borderColor": "#d1d5db"
                      }
                    }
                  ],
                  "isExpanded": true,
                  "parentId": "5aaf6c26-8187-4c87-a844-8266817f066d",
                  "data": {
                    "note": "**层** 证明\n\n**类型** inductive\n\n**模块** `Init.Prelude`\n\n**签名**\n```lean\nType u → ℕ → Type u\n```\n\n**文档**\nThe class `OfNat α n` powers the numeric literal parser. If you write\n`37 : α`, Lean will attempt to synthesize `OfNat α 37`, and will generate\nthe term `(OfNat.ofNat 37 : α)`.\n\nThere is a bit of infinite regress here since the desugaring apparently\nstill contains a literal `37` in it. The type of expressions contains a\nprimitive constructor for \"raw natural number literals\", which you can directly\naccess using the macro `nat_lit 37`. Raw number literals are always of type `Nat`.\nSo it would be more correct to say that Lean looks for an instance of\n`OfNat α (nat_lit 37)`, and it generates the term `(OfNat.ofNat (nat_lit 37) : α)`.",
                    "tags": [
                      "declaration",
                      "证明",
                      "inductive"
                    ]
                  },
                  "style": {
                    "background": "#f7fef9",
                    "color": "#14532d",
                    "fontSize": 13,
                    "borderColor": "#86efac"
                  }
                },
